# Adaptive MAS Operational Constraints

- Before any CUDA/GPU work, run `module load cuda12.6/toolkit/12.6`.
- Use the project virtualenv at `/local/yzheng/pnair/workspace/adaptive-mas/.venv`.
- Use the E5 model snapshot at `/local/yzheng/pnair/.cache/huggingface/models--intfloat--e5-base-v2/snapshots/f52bf8ec8c7124536f0efb74aca902b2995e5bcd`.
- Always compute contain and other metrics with `scripts/eval_offline.py`; do not trust ad-hoc contain scripts.
- Current system goal: build an EMNLP-ready adaptive topology RAG system for MuSiQue with roughly SAS efficiency and MAS performance.
- Target `contain >= 0.40`.
- Average tokens should ideally be about `10-15k` and must stay below `20k`.
- Do not use ensembling, pooling, or majority voting.
- Agents must use thinking.
- Subagents must retrieve internally; the orchestrator must never pass retrieved passages into subagent prompts.
- Evidence capsules may expose only answer, justification, confidence, support ids/snippets, and must not expose raw full passages.
